<title>BELGIUM: EU CLEARS TRAINING AID TO PHILIPS SEMICONDUCTOR.</title>
<headline>EU CLEARS TRAINING AID TO PHILIPS SEMICONDUCTOR.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission said on Wednesday it had cleared 8.6 million guilders in EU and Dutch subsidies to support a training program at Philips Semiconductor BV .</p>
<p>The project aims at &quot;retraining unemployed and employees threatened with unemployment&quot; in the region of Arnhem-Nijmegen, on the German border, where Philips built a new plant, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The money, of which 6.6 million guilders will be paid by the European Social Fund and the remaining by the province of Gelderland, is expected to lead to the creation of some 600 new jobs.</p>
<p>-- Brussels newsroom 322 2876841</p>
